275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Consultatation meeting and Household level holistic planning with farmers: On 20th March 2024, MOSONiE-Socio-Economic Foundation organized a consultation meeting and household level holistic planning with the farmers at Timbokgre Village. The meeting started with an introductory welcome by Lian from MOSONiE-SEF followed by a felicitation of the Resource person of the day. Romen Rabha from Diya Foundation was the resource person during the meeting.  The consultation meeting was mainly focus on economic, social, well being and happiness which involve a comprehensive planning that encompasses various aspects of life. He emphasized on the importance of striving for a better lifestyle through hard work. He illustrated with an example from an income perspective showing how increased the numbers of working individuals could lead to extra income for instance attending social functions or markets incurred an annual expenditure suggesting the need to double income for a healthier lifestyle. Additionally he also highlighted alternative source of income such as harvesting areca nut which could yield significant returns. He further elaborated on entrepreneurial opportunities in poultry farming including meet processing, making pickles form poultry products etc. The session focus on the practical activity where the participants were given a task on Household level holistic planning exercise using the format of Family Income and Expenditure flow chart.  The depth of understanding and experience shared by the resource person has brought broadened perspective and stimulated a meaning discussion within the group which contributes significant to the success of the meeting. Overall 19 farmers were participated during the meeting.)
/E (Consultatation meeting and Household level holistic planning with farmers: On 20th March 2024, MOSONiE-Socio-Economic Foundation organized a consultation meeting and household level holistic planning with the farmers at Timbokgre Village. The meeting started with an introductory welcome by Lian from MOSONiE-SEF followed by a felicitation of the Resource person of the day. Romen Rabha from Diya Foundation was the resource person during the meeting.  The consultation meeting was mainly focus on economic, social, well being and happiness which involve a comprehensive planning that encompasses various aspects of life. He emphasized on the importance of striving for a better lifestyle through hard work. He illustrated with an example from an income perspective showing how increased the numbers of working individuals could lead to extra income for instance attending social functions or markets incurred an annual expenditure suggesting the need to double income for a healthier lifestyle. Additionally he also highlighted alternative source of income such as harvesting areca nut which could yield significant returns. He further elaborated on entrepreneurial opportunities in poultry farming including meet processing, making pickles form poultry products etc. The session focus on the practical activity where the participants were given a task on Household level holistic planning exercise using the format of Family Income and Expenditure flow chart.  The depth of understanding and experience shared by the resource person has brought broadened perspective and stimulated a meaning discussion within the group which contributes significant to the success of the meeting. Overall 19 farmers were participated during the meeting.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
